  "directions": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "title": "Simmer",
      "text": "Simmer the heavy cream with a pinch of salt, the sugar, and the lemon zest for 3-5 minutes."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "title": "Set",
      "text": "Pull off the heat and whisk in the lemon juice. Rest 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "title": "Strain",
      "text": "Strain to pull the zest out. Microplaned zest is not pleasant to eat."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "title": "Freeze",
      "text": "Pour into ramekins (or hollowed-out lemon halves) and freeze about 4 hours. Serve straight from the freezer."
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Worth trying with other citrus. Lime is close to a straight swap. Blood orange would need its acid bumped — supplement with lemon juice — since it isn't tart enough on its own to set the cream."
  ],
  "deviations": [
    {
      "what": "Frozen instead of refrigerated",
      "why": "A traditional posset sets in the fridge into a soft, spoonable pudding. Freezing it gives a denser, custardy semi-frozen texture."
    },
    {
      "what": "Heavier on the lemon than a typical posset",
      "why": "Slightly more zest and juice than standard, pushing the lemon flavor further forward."
    }
  ],
